From: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
Date: Fri, 02 Oct 2026 18:08:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi-scripts: isolate bridged AP stations by default

The shell scripts set ap_isolate on every bridged AP unless
multicast_to_unicast was 0. The ucode scripts set it only when
multicast_to_unicast or proxy_arp is set explicitly. netifd still
turns on hairpin mode on the bridge port by default. With ap_isolate
off, mac80211 forwards frames between two stations on the same BSS
itself, and the frames never reach the bridge. Client isolation that
filters on the bridge then does not apply to these stations.

Restore the shell default: a bridged AP gets ap_isolate unless
multicast_to_unicast is 0. Frames between stations then go through
the bridge, which sends them back out through the hairpin port
unless a filter drops them.

Signed-off-by: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
---
 src/usr/share/ucode/wifi/ap.uc |    5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/usr/share/ucode/wifi/ap.uc
+++ b/src/usr/share/ucode/wifi/ap.uc
@@ -164,7 +164,10 @@ function iface_setup(config) {
 	else
 		append('bss', config.ifname);
 
-	if (config.multicast_to_unicast || config.proxy_arp)
+	/* netifd hairpins a bridged AP port unless multicast_to_unicast is off;
+	 * isolate the BSS to match, so station-to-station frames pass through
+	 * the bridge and its filters instead of mac80211 forwarding them */
+	if ((config.network_bridge && (config.multicast_to_unicast ?? true)) || config.proxy_arp)
 		config.ap_isolate = 1;
 
 	if (config.proxy_arp)
